Description: Wild OS start-up manager
 Chooses what a PC with more than one system starts. Holding Space while the
 PC starts shows a picture menu of Wild OS, Windows or another system on any
 disk, a USB stick that can start, and restore points. It can also show at
 every start with a countdown.
 .
 Other systems are looked for each time, on every disk, so one on a second
 disk or added later is found whether or not the PC's firmware lists it.
 Settings > System > Start-up disk sets what starts by default and restarts
 straight into another system.
 .
 The manager runs from Wild OS's own start-up files. GRUB stays the first
 thing the PC runs and is never seen.
